.TH ABRAFLEXI\-TUI 1 "2026-09-22" "abraflexi-tui 1.0.0" "AbraFlexi TUI Manual"
.SH NAME
abraflexi\-tui \- Turbo Vision text user interface for abraflexi\-cli
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B abraflexi\-tui
[\fB\-\-cli\fR=\fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-envfile\fR=\fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B abraflexi\-tui
is a text-mode (Turbo Vision / tvision) front end for
.BR abraflexi\-cli (1).
It never talks to the AbraFlexi REST API itself: every screen shells out to
.B abraflexi\-cli
with \fB\-\-format=json\fR and renders the result. Evidence-schema logic stays
in
.BR abraflexi\-cli .
Saved server profiles (URL, company, password or session token) live in
the TUI and are passed to the CLI as environment variables.
.PP
The browser is generic and evidence-parameterized: there is one record list
screen that works for any AbraFlexi evidence (picked from the evidence
browser), not a separate screen per evidence type.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-cli= PATH
Path to the
.B abraflexi\-cli
binary to run. Defaults to the value of \fBABRAFLEXI_TUI_CLI\fR, or
.B abraflexi\-cli
resolved from \fBPATH\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-envfile= FILE
Forwarded as \fB\-\-envfile\fR to
.B abraflexi\-cli
when no server profile is active. If omitted, \fBabraflexi\-cli\fR's own
default \fI.env\fR discovery applies. Once a profile is active, that
profile's variables are injected instead and \fB\-\-envfile\fR is not
forwarded.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/abraflexi\-tui/servers.json
Saved server profiles. Created mode 0600. \fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR overrides
.I ~/.config
when set. On the first start, if this file does not exist, a profile named
.B default
is imported from \fB\-\-envfile\fR or from inherited \fBABRAFLEXI_*\fR
variables when those provide \fBABRAFLEXI_URL\fR. When neither source
defines a server, a profile named
.B demo
is created for the public server
.B https://demo.flexibee.eu:5434
(login
.BR winstrom ,
company
.BR demo )
and made active.
If a profile is already active, the Status dialog is shown at startup.
If no profile is active, the Servers dialog is shown so a configuration
can be chosen.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/abraflexi\-tui/abraflexi\-tui.log
Failures from
.B abraflexi\-cli
(invalid JSON, a non-zero exit, or a missing binary). Each entry records the
command, the request URL, the exit code, and stdout and stderr. Created mode
0600. \fBXDG_STATE_HOME\fR overrides
.I ~/.local/state
when set.
.SH SCREENS
.TP
.B About (F1, Help menu)
Version and homepages of the libraries and utilities used by
.BR abraflexi\-tui :
.BR abraflexi\-cli ,
php-abraflexi, Turbo Vision (tvision), nlohmann/json and ncurses.
Enter or Open starts
.B xdg-open
on the selected address.
.TP
.B Status (Alt-S)
Shows the configured AbraFlexi connection and whether the server and
company are reachable (\fBabraflexi\-cli status\fR).
.TP
.B Companies (Alt-C)
Lists companies available on the server (\fBabraflexi\-cli list\-companies\fR).
Press Enter or double-click a row to choose that company. The status line
then shows its database name next to the query editor mode (\fBJSON\fR or
\fBXML\fR).
.TP
.B Evidences (Alt-E)
Lists available evidence catalogues (\fBabraflexi\-cli list\-evidences\fR).
Press Enter or double-click a row to open its record list. F2 shows
columns, relations and labels.
.TP
.B Record list
Generic, evidence-parameterized browser
(\fBabraflexi\-cli record \fIEVIDENCE\fB list\fR) with editable filter,
columns, limit and order fields, an F5 refresh, and an embedded detail
panel that follows the highlighted row. Press Enter on a row to fetch the
full record (\fBabraflexi\-cli record \fIEVIDENCE\fB show \fIID\fR).
Edit saves with
.BR "record update" ,
Delete removes the row after confirmation, and Info (F2) opens the
evidence structure.
.TP
.B New Record
Opens a JSON payload editor pre-annotated with the evidence's mandatory
fields (sourced from \fBabraflexi\-cli\fR's own validation output). Offers
Dry-Run and Submit, and a Force checkbox mapped to \fB\-\-force\fR.
.TP
.B Find (Alt-F)
Searches one evidence (\fBrecord \fIEVIDENCE\fB search\fR). With the
evidence field empty, filters evidence names from
.BR list\-evidences .
.TP
.B Query (Alt-Q)
Sends a raw REST request through
.B abraflexi\-cli query
(method, path, optional body). A relative path is placed under
.IR /c/COMPANY/ .
JSON or XML selects syntax highlighting for the body. The choice is stored
in
.I servers.json
and shown on the status line.
.TP
.B Changes (Alt-G)
Shows Changes API status and can enable or disable it, and register or
unregister a webhook. There is no HTTP listener; the registered URL must
already be reachable.
.TP
.B Servers (Alt-V)
Lists profiles stored in
.IR ~/.config/abraflexi\-tui/servers.json
(mode 0600). Add, edit, delete and set the active profile. Enter or
double-click on a profile makes it active and opens the status dialog.
Password
profiles inject
.B ABRAFLEXI_LOGIN
and
.BR ABRAFLEXI_PASSWORD ;
token profiles inject
.B ABRAFLEXI_AUTHSESSID
and clear the password variables.
.B Get Token...
calls
.B abraflexi\-cli login
with the values typed in the form and does not write them until OK.
The status line shows the AbraFlexi URL implied by the request in progress.
.PP
PDF preview, company backup, restore, clone and reset, the custom-button
designer and a webhook HTTP listener remain in Flexplorer.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ABRAFLEXI_TUI_CLI
Path to the \fBabraflexi\-cli\fR binary to run; overridden by \fB\-\-cli\fR.
.PP
When a server profile is active, the TUI sets
.BR ABRAFLEXI_URL ,
.BR ABRAFLEXI_COMPANY ,
and either
.BR ABRAFLEXI_LOGIN / ABRAFLEXI_PASSWORD
or
.B ABRAFLEXI_AUTHSESSID
in the CLI child. Otherwise those variables are read by
.B abraflexi\-cli
itself; see
.BR abraflexi\-cli (1).
.PP
Session tokens are not refreshed in the background. If a token expires,
request a new one with
.B Get Token...
on the Servers screen.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit (Alt-X / Quit).
.SH EXAMPLES
Run against the system-installed CLI and default \fI.env\fR discovery:
.RS
.EX
abraflexi\-tui
.EE
.RE
.PP
Run against a CLI checkout and an explicit environment file:
.RS
.EX
ABRAFLEXI_TUI_CLI=./abraflexi\-cli/bin/abraflexi\-cli \e
    abraflexi\-tui \-\-envfile=./abraflexi\-cli/.env
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR abraflexi\-cli (1)
